    {
      "lesson_num": 1,
      "section_type": "Conversation",
      "title": "Meeting a Foreign Student",
      "content": "Ali: 'Hello! What is your name?' Jean: 'My name is Jean.' Ali: 'Are you from France?' Jean: 'Yes, I am French, but I live in Spain now. Where are you from?' Ali: 'I am from Iran. I live in Shiraz. Welcome to our country!'"
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 1,
      "section_type": "Reading",
      "title": "My Homeland Iran",
      "content": "Iran is a wonderful country in Asia. It has an ancient culture and friendly people. Millions of people speak Persian. Many tourists visit Iranian cities every year to see historical places."
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 2,
      "section_type": "Conversation",
      "title": "Weekly School Routine",
      "content": "Nima: 'What do you do on Saturday mornings, Reza?' Reza: 'I go to school and have English and science classes.' Nima: 'Do you study on Thursdays?' Reza: 'No, on Thursday afternoons I go to the gym and play volleyball with my classmates.'"
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 2,
      "section_type": "Reading",
      "title": "A Busy Weekday",
      "content": "In Iran, students attend school from Saturday to Wednesday. Thursday and Friday are the weekend. On weekdays, children wake up early, eat breakfast, and study their school lessons. On Friday, families gather together for lunch."
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 3,
      "section_type": "Conversation",
      "title": "Talking about Talents and Abilities",
      "content": "Teacher: 'Who can recite the Holy Quran beautifully in our class?' Sara: 'Maryam can recite it very well, teacher.' Teacher: 'That is wonderful! Can you speak English, Maryam?' Maryam: 'Yes, I can speak English and I can write short stories, too.'"
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 3,
      "section_type": "Reading",
      "title": "Sports and Talents",
      "content": "Every student has different talents. Some students can swim and ride bicycles fast. Others can draw colorful pictures or play chess. Developing healthy abilities makes young students confident."
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 4,
      "section_type": "Conversation",
      "title": "At the School Clinic",
      "content": "Health Teacher: 'What is the matter, Sina? You look pale.' Sina: 'I have a terrible toothache and a headache.' Health Teacher: 'You should rest in the clinic for an hour. Then you should see a dentist this afternoon.' Sina: 'Thank you, teacher.'"
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 4,
      "section_type": "Reading",
      "title": "Taking Care of Your Health",
      "content": "Good health is very important for all people. When you have a cold, cough, or fever, you should drink warm tea and rest in bed. Eating fresh vegetables and exercising every day helps prevent illnesses."
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 5,
      "section_type": "Conversation",
      "title": "Describing Shiraz",
      "content": "Tourist: 'Excuse me, where is Shiraz located?' Guide: 'It is located in the south of Iran.' Tourist: 'What is it famous for?' Guide: 'It is famous for the tombs of Hafez and Saadi, magnificent gardens, and hospitable people.'"
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 5,
      "section_type": "Reading",
      "title": "Historical Cities of Iran",
      "content": "Iran has many famous cities. Isfahan is in the center of Iran and is famous for historic bridges and mosques. Mashhad is a holy city in the northeast. Shiraz is in the south and attracts lovers of Persian culture."
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 6,
      "section_type": "Conversation",
      "title": "Visiting a Green Village",
      "content": "Babak: 'Is your grandfather's village far from here, Omid?' Omid: 'No, it is near the mountain. It has clean air and a beautiful river.' Babak: 'What do villagers do?' Omid: 'Most villagers are farmers. They raise cattle and grow wheat and rice.'"
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 6,
      "section_type": "Reading",
      "title": "Life in an Iranian Village",
      "content": "Life in a village is quiet and peaceful. There is no traffic or air pollution. Farmers wake up at sunrise to work in the green fields. They raise domestic animals and produce fresh milk, butter, and bread."
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 7,
      "section_type": "Conversation",
      "title": "Talking about Weekend Hobbies",
      "content": "Farhad: 'What do you do in your free time, Kian?' Kian: 'I enjoy reading books and playing tennis.' Farhad: 'Do you play computer games, too?' Kian: 'Sometimes on weekends, but I prefer outdoor sports in the park.'"
    },
    {
      "lesson_num": 7,
      "section_type": "Reading",
      "title": "Healthy Hobbies",
      "content": "Having an enjoyable hobby helps reduce daily stress. Reading books opens our minds to new knowledge. Playing sports like football keeps our bodies fit. Spending time on constructive hobbies makes life happy."
    }
  ],
